## 👋 About me

I am a software developer focused on building real-world applications from the domain model to the user interface. My strongest area is **ASP.NET Core backend and full-stack development**, complemented by hands-on experience with **Angular**, **Razor Pages**, **Flutter/Dart**, and **Python computer vision and speech processing**.

I enjoy solving workflow-heavy problems: understanding the business rules, designing a maintainable architecture, protecting data with proper authorization, and delivering software that people can actually use.

## ⭐ Main project: Accountant3 / YAccountant

<div align="center">

### A financial management platform for budgets, expenses, centers, approvals, and reporting

[![Open Accountant3](https://img.shields.io/badge/Explore_Accountant3-View_Repository-512BD4?style=for-the-badge&logo=github&logoColor=white)](https://github.com/sunn789/accountant3)

</div>

Accountant3 is my main and most complete application. It is a multi-layer financial and administrative platform built to manage organizational centers, budgets, allocations, expenses, users, approvals, dashboards, and reports.

### What I developed

| Area | Capabilities |
|---|---|
| **Backend API** | ASP.NET Core REST API for budgets, adjustments, expenses, items, centers, users, dashboards, reports, and payments |
| **Business workflows** | Monthly expense registration, editing, approval, deletion, debt details, budget locking, and yearly summaries |
| **Security** | JWT authentication, ASP.NET Core Identity, roles, claims, authorization policies, and center-scoped access |
| **Angular UI** | Authenticated routing, lazy-loaded features, route guards, role guards, HTTP interceptors, dashboards, user management, centers, and budget screens |
| **Razor UI** | Server-rendered administration and financial workflow pages with Identity integration |
| **Operations** | Health checks, database initialization, migrations, validation, pagination, centralized API responses, and OpenAPI/Scalar documentation |

### Architecture

Accountant3 is structured around **Clean Architecture** with clear boundaries between:

```text
API  →  Application  →  Core / Domain
          ↓                 ↑
     Infrastructure  ←  Contracts
          ↓
   SQL Server / SQLite

Angular UI + Razor Pages UI
```

Application features follow a **Vertical Slice / feature-oriented structure**. Commands, queries, handlers, validators, DTOs, mappings, and related behavior stay close to the use case they implement. This keeps the codebase easier to navigate, test, extend, and maintain.

